      "line": 256,
      "code": "INPUT_BYTE(cinfo, cinfo->num_components, return FALSE);",
      "note": "First project-code read that creates vulnerability-relevant JPEG state: `get_sof()` pulls the component count from the recovered SOF header. For the staged witness this byte is `3`, which sizes the later `coef_bits` / `prev_coef_bits` tables and the all-component smoothing loops.",
      "kind": "source"
    },
    {
      "file": "jdphuff.c",
      "function": "start_pass_phuff_decoder",
      "line": null,
      "code": "for (coefi = MIN(cinfo->Ss, 1); coefi <= MAX(cinfo->Se, 9); coefi++) { if (cinfo->input_scan_number > 1) prev_coef_bit_ptr[coefi] = coef_bit_ptr[coefi]; }",
      "note": "On the first progressive Huffman scan, this loop has no `else` initialization for `prev_coef_bit_ptr[coefi]` when `input_scan_number == 1`. The step therefore leaves each component's `prev_coef_bits[1..9]` undefined even though later block-smoothing code assumes those previous-scan entries are initialized. The fix patch adds `else prev_coef_bit_ptr[coefi] = 0;` at this exact site; the recovered witness JPEG uses `SOF2`/`FFC4`, so the `jdphuff.c` side of the patch is the executed root cause.",
      "kind": "root_cause_function"
